invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20_vector.h
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: chacha20_vector.h no longer stops a big-endian build. There a
  keystream word leaves its lane in big-endian byte order, which is not
  the order RFC 8439 serializes in, so every block would be wrong. No
  runner here is big-endian, so no vector could catch it; the script
  compiles the header for big-endian AArch64 with the pinned clang and
  requires the refusal.

--- old
#if !defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) || __BYTE_ORDER__ != __ORDER_LITTLE_ENDIAN__
--- new
#if 0
